2Z","closed_at":"2026-03-07T11:36:36Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8088) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-14700K (28 threads) - 47.72 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nA match on a previous line, at the same column position, will be skipped when pressing Previous Match.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b4891ca0-a731-44d8-81e7-2e1ee961b444\n\n`print(3);` is skipped\n\nI believe this is an issue in the implementation of the `search` function in `text_edit.cpp` regarding clamping of columns.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nPut this in a Godot .gd file in the editor:\n\n```\nextends Node\n\nfunc _ready():\n    print(1)\n    \n    print(2)\n    \n    print(3)\n    print(4)\n    \n    print(5)\n```\n\nThen see above repro video.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"MattParkerDev","id":61717342,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzE3MzQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61717342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev","html_url":"https://github.com/MattParkerDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.